# Build after changes

When a task changes project files, finish by running:

```bash
npm run build
```

- Run it once, after the edits are done, not after every intermediate save.
- If the build fails, fix the cause and run it again until it succeeds.
- Skip the build only when the task did not change any project files.

# Commits

After `npm run build` succeeds, create local commits (never push):

1. In this repository (`Harrix-HTML-Template`): commit only the agent's changed/added/deleted files plus updated build outputs from this task, using the usual `# Git style` title.
2. If `D:\GitHub\Harrix-HTML-Template-dist-history` has changes produced by `npm run build`, create a matching local commit there with the **same** commit title (agent/build outputs only; never push).

At the end, show both created commit titles and short hashes. If a commit could not be created, show the intended title and the reason.
